1. What was your primary contribution to the project?
My main contribution was developing the C program, including temperature monitoring, configurable ranges, average calculations, file saving, and test cases. My partner handled the Raspberry Pi hardware setup.

2. What was the most challenging technical problem?
The biggest challenge was running the C program in different environments, especially when the online compiler could not recognize the Raspberry Pi’s pigpio library.

3. How did your team use testing or debugging to solve a problem?
We tested different temperatures to verify the NORMAL and WARNING statuses. I also used simulation mode to resolve the compiler issue and test the program without the Raspberry Pi.

4. Which skills from CSE 1106 were most useful?
The most useful skills were learning how to use GitHub properly, working with the Raspberry Pi, and using PowerShell. These helped me understand coding, hardware integration, and project collaboration.

5. What would you improve if you had more time?
I would create a more user-friendly interface, add an automatic temperature sensor, and improve the data logging system by including timestamps.

